# Append-only shared records. Parallel slices add lines at the same anchor of
# these files; a textual conflict between two such additions means "keep both",
# never "pick one". `merge=union` makes `git rebase`/`git merge` keep both sides
# locally (GitHub's own conflict check does not read this file, so a re-parented
# branch still has to be pushed). `scripts/check_union_merge.py` refuses the
# one thing a union can get wrong: a duplicated bullet or heading.
openspec/changes/*/tasks.md merge=union
rust/README.md merge=union

# Large binaries and frozen fixtures, tracked by Git LFS from this commit
# forward. History is not rewritten. Patterns stay narrow so the small fixtures
# under rust/tests/ stay ordinary Git objects. Jobs that read these bytes run
# `git lfs pull` after checkout (the same step as actions/checkout `lfs: true`).
*.systrace filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.htrace filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
Packages/ArkDeckKit/ThirdParty/TraceStreamer/macx/trace_streamer filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
rust/tests/fixtures/device-mutation-reconcile-native-published-c6-v4/oracle.json filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
rust/tests/fixtures/device-mutation-reconcile-native-published-c6-v4/raw-oracle.json filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Generated sources. GitHub Linguist should not treat them as handwritten code.
windows/App.Core/Generated/UiStrings.g.cs linguist-generated=true
windows/ClientKit/Generated/ControlContract.g.cs linguist-generated=true

